  "prefLabel": "Env-A 618.05 Implementation Plan Requirements",
  "priorExpiration": "2011-10-24",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 618.05 Implementation Plan Requirements. In accordance with section 173(a)(4) of the Act, the department shall not issue a permit or permits to a stationary source to which the requirements of this part apply if the administrator has determined that the applicable implementation plan is not being adequately implemented for the nonattainment area in which the proposed source is to be constructed or modified.\n\nSource. #7879, eff 4-26-03 (formerly Env-A 622.05(c)(5)-(d)); amd by #9791, eff 10-1-10; amd by #9906, INTERIM, eff 4-26-11, EXPIRES: 10-24-11; ss by #10000, eff 10-1-11; ss by #10175, eff 9-1-12 (from Env-A 618.06); ss by #13510, eff 12-17-22",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a600.html"
